          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Looks well and is talking clearly."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left scrotal symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports left scrotal swelling present for months, previously described to him as a fluid sac around the testicle. Over the last 3–4 days it has felt slightly larger and more uncomfortable, with a dull ache or dragging sensation in the left hemiscrotum, worse after standing all day. No sudden severe pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Partner-reported behavior and mobility change"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Partner reports patient has been “not himself” for 3–4 days, guarding his groin, and walking differently for the last 2 days."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood and irritability"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient describes feeling “a bit on edge and cranky,” especially in the evenings after work, and thinks this is probably because the scrotum is sore and annoying. Denies low mood, anxiety, and new stressors."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported associated symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, dysuria, urinary frequency, haematuria, penile discharge, fevers, rigors, weight loss, night sweats, trauma, and lifting more than usual. Patient has not noticed a groin lump extending into the canal or a cough impulse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft and non-tender, with no masses."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Inguinal and femoral hernia examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No palpable inguinal or femoral hernia on cough."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Left hemiscrotum enlarged, smooth, and without erythema. Fluctuant, non-tender swelling around the left testis that transilluminates strongly. Left testis palpable within the swelling but difficult to delineate fully; normal where felt, with no discrete lump."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right testicular examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right testis normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Additional scrotal and inguinal examination findings"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No epididymal tenderness, varicocele, increased warmth, or inguinal lymphadenopathy."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mental status and behavior"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert, oriented, and coherent. Mood described as “a bit irritable”; affect appropriate. No psychotic features. Calm and cooperative during consultation."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
